22
00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:54.000
and babies often are cutting teeth or they get sick or they just don't feel like participating in your study the day you need them to laugh. They're in a terrible mood. So we do well to follow them. You know, we've done only one study where we followed them from three months to 12 months. And it was incredibly laborious. We're glad we did it. But yet right now we're just doing some point in time studies. But we have done some from six to 12 months. Usually I don't go past that point. I have a great colleague at the University of Bristol in the UK who studies joke-telling and toddlers. So she sort of picks up where I left off or vice versa. Are there cultural differences or do all babies manifest humor at about the same time

